§ `Words and phrases: Civ. Code § 13, Code Civ. Proc. § 16`

-- Neither limb: the context and the approved usage of the language.
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Civil Code` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` FALSE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` FALSE EQUALS `the context and the approved usage of the language`
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` FALSE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` FALSE EQUALS `the context and the approved usage of the language`
-- Either limb, or both: the peculiar and appropriate meaning or the definition.
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Civil Code` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` TRUE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` FALSE EQUALS `the peculiar and appropriate meaning in law, or the definition in the succeeding section`
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Civil Code` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` FALSE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` TRUE EQUALS `the peculiar and appropriate meaning in law, or the definition in the succeeding section`
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Civil Code` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` TRUE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` TRUE EQUALS `the peculiar and appropriate meaning in law, or the definition in the succeeding section`
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` TRUE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` FALSE EQUALS `the peculiar and appropriate meaning in law, or the definition in the succeeding section`
#ASSERT `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` FALSE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` TRUE EQUALS `the peculiar and appropriate meaning in law, or the definition in the succeeding section`
-- Outside the encoding: the Government Code has no such section in the deposit.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the source of the meaning of a word or phrase, in` `the Government Code` `given that it is technical or peculiar:` TRUE `and that it is defined in the succeeding section:` FALSE

§ `Strict and liberal construction: Civ. Code § 4, Code Civ. Proc. § 4`

#ASSERT NOT (`the common-law rule of strict construction of statutes in derogation of it applies to the code` `the Civil Code`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the common-law rule of strict construction of statutes in derogation of it applies to the code` `the Code of Civil Procedure`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the common-law rule of strict construction of statutes in derogation of it applies to the code` `the Government Code`
#ASSERT `the approach to construing` `a provision of the code` `in` `the Civil Code` EQUALS liberal
#ASSERT `the approach to construing` `a provision of the code` `in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` EQUALS liberal
#ASSERT `the approach to construing` `a proceeding under the code` `in` `the Code of Civil Procedure` EQUALS liberal
-- Civ. Code § 4 does not mention proceedings; neither section speaks of a statute outside its code; the Government Code has no such section.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the approach to construing` `a proceeding under the code` `in` `the Civil Code`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the approach to construing` `a statute in derogation of the common law that is outside the code` `in` `the Civil Code`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the approach to construing` `a statute in derogation of the common law that is outside the code` `in` `the Code of Civil Procedure`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the approach to construing` `a provision of the code` `in` `the Government Code`
#ASSERT `the code establishes the law of this State on the subject` `the Civil Code` `given that the subject is one to which the code relates:` TRUE
#ASSERT `the code establishes the law of this State on the subject` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `given that the subject is one to which the code relates:` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the code establishes the law of this State on the subject` `the Civil Code` `given that the subject is one to which the code relates:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the code establishes the law of this State on the subject` `the Government Code` `given that the subject is one to which the code relates:` TRUE

§ `Gov. Code § 23: severability`

#ASSERT NOT (`the remainder of the code is affected when held invalid is` `a provision of the code`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application of the provision to other persons or circumstances is affected when held invalid is` `the application of a provision to a person or circumstance`)
-- The text pairs each holding with one consequence; the crossed cases are not said.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the remainder of the code is affected when held invalid is` `the application of a provision to a person or circumstance`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the application of the provision to other persons or circumstances is affected when held invalid is` `a provision of the code`

§ `Gov. Code § 12.5 and § 24: the words man and workmen's compensation`

#ASSERT `the term deemed in place of` "man" `where it is appropriate:` TRUE EQUALS "person"
#ASSERT `the term deemed in place of` "men" `where it is appropriate:` TRUE EQUALS "persons"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term deemed in place of` "man" `where it is appropriate:` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term deemed in place of` "woman" `where it is appropriate:` TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to the term man or men is to be changed to person or persons` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to the term man or men is to be changed to person or persons` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the term also known as` "workmen's compensation" EQUALS "workers' compensation"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the term also known as` "workers' compensation"
#ASSERT `a reference to workmen's compensation is to be changed to workers' compensation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to workmen's compensation is to be changed to workers' compensation` FALSE)

§ `Civ. Code § 22 and § 22.1: law and the will of the supreme power`

#ASSERT `an expression is a law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an expression is a law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an expression is a law` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`an expression is a law` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the will of the supreme power is expressed by` `the Constitution`
#ASSERT `the will of the supreme power is expressed by` `a statute`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the will of the supreme power is expressed by` `something else`

§ `Gov. Code § 9603: where the general rules are`

#ASSERT `the preliminary provisions of the code contain general rules for the construction of statutes` `the Government Code`
#ASSERT `the preliminary provisions of the code contain general rules for the construction of statutes` `the Civil Code`
#ASSERT `the preliminary provisions of the code contain general rules for the construction of statutes` `the Code of Civil Procedure`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the general rules for the construction of a statute that is in no code are in`

